      "writtenOn": "2025-12-03T22:29:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One alternative that I can see is to update `UnmapInternal` and `Unmap` to take an additional argument that determines whether we need do the `CopyFromStagingBuffer` call since I think that\u0027s the only \"optimization\" that we do when we do the unmap inside of a destroy. I think if we do that, then the loop just becomes:\n\n```\ncase BufferState::Mapped:\ncase BufferState::PendingMap:\ncase BufferState::MappedAtCreation:\n    UnmapInternal(..., /*forDestroy\u003d*/true);\n    break;\ncase BufferState::InsideOperation:\n    mState.wait(BufferState::InsideOperation, std::memory_order_acquire);\n    break;\ncase BufferState::Unmapped:\ncase BufferState::Destroyed\ndefault:\n    break;\n```\n\nAnd then in `Unmap`, we just conditionally call `CopyFromStagingBuffer` versus just nulling it out.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 465,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 466,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "bb9b223143fdf2880059d36f60f068655e48a4e0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
